There are not a lot of people who know anything about asbestos.
In fact, asbestos isn't an asbestos one substance, it's a group of six minerals.
It was named due to its fibrous structure, which gives him strength and flexibility.
Of the six Minerals, three have been used in the construction industry.
Most often it is now possible to find chrysotile in buildings, commonly known as white asbestos.
It was used in roofing panels, floor tiles, boiler seals and even brake lining.
It is not as deadly as other forms of asbestos, the EU and the WHO nevertheless consider it a "great health risk" that can cause death.
More Dangerous are brown asbestos (amosite) and blue asbestos (crocydolite).
Britain was once the world's largest importer of brown asbestos, and experts say "there is persuasive but circumstasory evidence that this was the main cause of an unusually-stricked occurrence of mesothelioma [in the United Kingdom). "
