The Goddard Consulting report, which explored Westminster's palace, shows that even people in the middle of the government may not have to know that they may be exudiated by asbestos.
In 2009, Goddard published a report that service elevators and pipes behind the parliamentary committee's rooms are contaminated with asbestos whose lethal filaments could be violated by something as harmless as "strong airflow."
