Prague raises new taxi patrol managers, earns 12.3 million
Prague has finalized tenders for new administrators of taxi stations.
It receives approximately CZK 12.3 million a year for 103 parking spaces.
Until recently, it collected 150 thousand crowns a year for the same seats for taxi drivers.
This was reported by Councilman Lukáš Manhart (TOP 09).
Earlier, the city used a draw when selecting administrators.
The winner then received a lease for a lump-sum amount of 1000 crowns per year.
But the rules have changed.
At the same time, the amount of the offer decides.
"The year since the denunciation of the original lease agreements and the opening of tenders, it has been proven that the new leasing system is much more advantageous for Prague and generally more eloquent," the councillor said.
Expensive spot is Na Perštýně
The highest price was offered by those interested in a station in Na Perštýně street.
It pays 2.1 million crowns a year.
Approximately CZK 1.5 million was Paid by the new administrators for the places in front of the Municipal Domicile or on Wenceslas Square.
In the autumn of 2012, councillors accepted the new rules of leases of taxi stations and terminated the original lease agreements in the summer of last year.
Tenders took place in four habres and a new administrator found 29 stations.
