Wasted employee took revenge, bought laptops for the company and sold them
After his dismissusion, the disgrundied employee bought computers for the company and then sold them.
He managed to spend the money before he was deceased.
In a short period of time, the man purchased a total of sixteen computers for more than two hundred thousand crowns.
"He transported the laptops after the takeover to Olomouc, where they were sold after bazaars," said Rostislav Brückner, Chief Commissioner of Šumperk.
The motive for the scavenger was revenge on the employer for the dismissal as well as the profit of the money.
"When interrogated, he told us that he used the money to repay loans," Brückner said.
Police also found that the impostor is a pathological player who was repeatedly treated in psychiatry.
Thus, the money could also end up in gaming devices or video lottery terminals.
"The fact is that we didn't find any money with him," the commissioner said.
An impraider, who has already been punished once for the theft, is now at risk of imprisonment between one and five years.
So far, the police have not said whether there is also a risk of punishment for bazaars who bought the laptops under the price and continued to sell them.
"It is true that they took over completely new merchandise, which is at least suspicious," the commissioner said.
However, none of the bazaar's owners have yet been charged.
