The Jewish Torah, the Christian Gospel, the Islamic Qur', the Bahá'u'lláh's Kitab-I-Akdas, Zarathuštrov Avesta, Sikh Adi-Granth, Mahabharat Bhagavad-Gita, the Book of Mormon, or the Book of Urantia are all considered "absolute truth" and the "revealed word of one true god".
