Kalabiña branch of the mafia is seen by the view of family relationships between clans who struggle for power and money with each other, the director was able to reconcile all presumptuous assumptions for a good film: high-quality script, camera, music and actor.
He was also captivativated by chamber psychothriller Hunger Hearts filmed Saverio Costanzo with Alba Rohrwacher in the role of a woman who almost kills her own child with his misleading anxieousness.
Conversely, there was no warm acceptance of the Familiar Familiarity for Familiar, nor 3 hearts, both works clinging to a traditional model of consumer films that rely on the popularity of academies.
But after all, after all, two really excellent films, i.e. Birdman and the Black Soul, are not so low for the first half of the festival.
And although festival films generally have depressing themes, Peter Bogdanovich's new film called She's Funny That Way, a witty comedy presented in Venice out-of-competition and shot in the style of the American merry-go-round of the 40's, managed to elevate the mood for more than a day.
