If we play like that since the beginning of the season, I'm convinced that we haven't lost yet," thinks Lébr.
Sigma in Opava withstood the introductory pressure of the home team, then leveled the game and in the second half it was already better.
After the victory, Kalvod's wards scored, but they didn't bring their options to the goal, so they couldn't win.
Although the result does not go according to our ideas.
To the full satisfaction, however, we lacked only one transformed chance," said Lébr, who does not think that the change in the approach of the footballers was caused only by his threat.
I'm sure there were more aspects.
Whether from my side, on the part of the coach or the fans," Lébr said.
Sigma has to reckon with the pressure
The players did not want to comment very much after the match in Opava last week's event.
I'm trying to put these things completely away.
I was trying not to admit it," young goalkeeper Michal Reichl shook his head.
Absolutely uncomfortably left a question about Lébro's statement last week striker Vaclav Vasicek, who didn't change Sigma's biggest opportunity in Saturday's match.
After all, he talked a little bit about the pressure.
We'll be under pressure all the time.
They're all wanting to pull on us.
Today we've shown that if we're going to fight and we're going to fuck everyone, we're going to," he said.
They took the warning to the heart
Even coach Leoš Kalvod didn't hide the fact that the preparation for the match wasn't the simplest due to the atmosphere that prevailed in Olomouc last week.
It's been pretty hard.
But I don't think the boys realized it, and today it was obvious that Mr. Lébro's warnings were taken to heart.
“Although it wasn’t even before that they didn’t want to fight and shove it away,” he said.
It used to be the first fifteen minutes.
It's been a long time to cope with hardness and realize what the second league was all about.
That it's not just about football, it's all about football," Kalvoda said.
All we have to do is hope that Sigma will work from the beginning in the next matches.
"I'd love to believe it," he added.
